<title>THAILAND: One Holding says default on B/E repayment.</title>
<headline>One Holding says default on B/E repayment.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's One Holding Plc said on Wednesday it had defaulted on $13.5 million due on its bill of exchange (B/E) payment because of a liquidity problem.</p>
<p>The two tranches of B/E worth $1 million and $12.5 million were due to be repaid on March 17 and 18, respectively, One Holding said in a filing to the Stock Exchange of Thailand.</p>
<p>One Holding is an investment arm of Finance One Plc.</p>
